From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmtksdio: drop the firmware's debug channel
 quietly

The combo firmware sends packet type 0x80 down the Bluetooth function when
it has something to report, core dumps included: after a Wi-Fi firmware
assert, several hundred packets in seconds. btmtksdio logs each as an
error, and on a 115200 serial console every line takes milliseconds spent
holding the SDIO host the Wi-Fi function shares, long enough to stall it.

Drop the channel quietly, and log one error a minute when a core dump is
seen, which vendor event 0xfc6f marks.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
index 5ee35d1..fbf72ec 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
@@ -445,6 +445,12 @@ static const struct h4_recv_pkt mtk_recv_pkts[] = {
 	{ H4_RECV_EVENT,    .recv = btmtksdio_recv_event },
 };
 
+/* The MT7668 combo firmware's debug channel, which its own driver drops. A
+ * core dump comes down it, each packet opening with a vendor event, 0xfc6f.
+ */
+#define MTK_SDIO_FW_DEBUG	0x80
+#define MTK_SDIO_FW_DUMP	0xfc6f
+
 static int btmtksdio_rx_packet(struct btmtksdio_dev *bdev, u16 rx_size)
 {
 	const struct h4_recv_pkt *pkts = mtk_recv_pkts;
@@ -485,6 +491,21 @@ static int btmtksdio_rx_packet(struct btmtksdio_dev *bdev, u16 rx_size)
 	/* Remove MediaTek SDIO header */
 	skb_pull(skb, sizeof(*sdio_hdr));
 
+	if (bdev->data->chipid == 0x7668 &&
+	    sdio_hdr->bt_type == MTK_SDIO_FW_DEBUG) {
+		static DEFINE_RATELIMIT_STATE(dump_rs, 60 * HZ, 1);
+
+		/* logged per packet, a dump holds the shared host long
+		 * enough to starve the other function
+		 */
+		if (skb->len >= 6 &&
+		    get_unaligned_le16(skb->data + 4) == MTK_SDIO_FW_DUMP &&
+		    __ratelimit(&dump_rs))
+			bt_dev_err(bdev->hdev, "firmware core dump");
+		kfree_skb(skb);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/* We have to dig into the packet to get payload size and then know how
 	 * many padding bytes at the tail, these padding bytes should be removed
 	 * before the packet is indicated to the core layer.
